{
  "record": "glm-margin-sample-size-sweep-v1",
  "date": "2026-11-21",
  "question": "Is the kmer mode's unresolved winnable region a sample-size problem that the unused 3140 promoter windows would fix?",
  "prediction": {
    "registered_before_any_number": true,
    "null": "RISES with more natural windows, because the committed geometry trains ~352 features on ~360 rows and is close to p=n, so added rows convert fitted split noise into real signal",
    "floor": "stays near 0.50 with SHRINKING spread, because real-versus-real has a true AUROC of 0.5 at every sample size and only its sampling variation depends on n",
    "margin": "mean rises and sd falls, so kmer becomes resolvable at some geometry IF the margin is real",
    "the_informative_failure": "a kmer margin that stays unresolved while its error bar visibly shrinks is evidence the margin is genuinely near zero, which would settle the kmer question in the opposite direction"
  },
  "geometry_note": "DELIBERATELY OFF the committed geometry. limit_natural moves the Markov fit size, the discriminator's train and test sizes and the class balance together; n_generated moves the balance again. These numbers must NEVER be joined to the committed grid's generator figures. The first config IS the committed cell and is flagged as such.",
