  "honest_limits": [
    "Five geometries on a coarse grid, not a fitted curve. It shows the DIRECTION the margin moves with data; it does not identify the sample size at which a mode becomes usable.",
    "limit_natural and n_generated are not separated: each config moves fit size, train size, test size and class balance at once. A clean separation would need a factorial over fit-n and eval-n, which this does not run.",
    "The floor is EMPIRICAL at one draw per seed. Its true value is 0.5 by construction for real-versus-real, so its mean is a check on the instrument and its SD is the quantity of interest here.",
    "Ten seeds per config, so each interval is itself imprecise; the resolvability flag is a reading of an interval, not a power calculation.",
    "The null is the Markov chain, which is refitted at each limit on a larger fit half, so a rising null mixes 'the discriminator sees more' with 'the null is fitted better'. Both push in the same direction here, and the sweep does not separate them.",
    "A winnable region is necessary, NOT sufficient: these features see LOCAL composition only.",
    "One organism, one null, one window length."
  ],
